  "id": "corollary-discharge",
  "term": "corollary discharge",
  "definition": "Corollary discharge is a mechanism thought to help the brain tell apart internally generated events from outside stimuli, such as distinguishing self-initiated sounds from external ones. In this context, it is studied through changes in evoked brain responses to self-generated auditory events.",
